A||||7||Blazin_Low02||Igniters?||||1||
Z||000000||Blazin_Low02||09-17-2001||11:09 PM||||Ok... I want to add an ingition system to shoot flames out my tail pipes. I know this can be achieved by puttin spark plugs in your exhaust tips.... but.. I want to add one coil for each plug.. and then run it down. Would this work? What would it take to add 2 coils? Thanks<P>~James<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT<BR>4 Clicker <BR>White face gauges, blue backlighting, custom marble dash, KYB and Koni, Eibach lowering springs, CD player, Kenwood 4x10's, clarion 4x6 plates, accel coil, aceel race wires, Archie V8 hood scoop, IRM rocker scoops, 1/4 window scoops!<P>Soon to have :150 shot of NOS, and a T3 turbo install||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-18-2001||12:14 AM||||that shouldnt be a prob, just put a switch in for each one. dont forget youll have to plumb a fuel line too. Be carefull or your Fiero will roast. I knew a guy that did that to twin stacks up the back of his pickup cab. The body filler on roof caught fire.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tryxalon||09-18-2001||07:31 AM||||It isn't smart, but here: <P>You don't need a coil since all you have to do is "spark" to ignite the unburned fuel in your exhaust. (yes, even with all the emissions control, there is still unburned fuel)<P>Just drill a hole in the tailpipe, screw a sparkplug into it, run a 12v "hot" wire from a "momentary on" switch to the top of the sparkplug.  Exhaust system forms a ground for the circuit. Switch on while the engine is running and you get "Flame on". <P>Actually, this is a dangerous idea, but you sound determined to do it.  Be careful though, because you may catch things like grass, paper, people nearby and even your car on fire. <P>oh, and stock up on tail pipes, you'll burn them out quickly, maybe as quick as 10 "shots" per.  <P>A<p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||09-18-2001||08:06 AM||||You cannot do this with a 12 volt wire.  You would have to make the gap for the plug way to small.  The reason for the coil is to make the voltage high enough to create a spark across the gap.  All you need to do is get an old ignition coil (imports have tiny ones) and run a switch from 12v to the one side of the primary. Ground the other side.  On the secondary ground one side and run the other to the plug.  Remember some coils are polarized so you may have to experiment to get the best spark.  For the flame to work you have to rev the engine and fire it while letting off the throttle.   I would suggest hitting the button multiple times quickly.  What I would do is hook up 2 555 timers to do the job.  One in oscillating squarewave mode and mone as a one shot mode.  Kick off the oneshot with the switch and have it control the oscillator for like 5 seconds. Go through a capacitor to the coil.  This would maintain a continuous spark for 5 seconds while you rev the engine and let off.  Its a very simple circuit and you can find the 555's and a book on how to hook them up at radioshack.  If you go this way check the primary resistance on the coil and adjust the "high" (where the squarewave is at 12v instead of 0v)time of the oscillator to a lower time so that the 555 does not get to hot.  Of course you can do the low tech way and just keep pushing the switch but might as well make it automatic.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||09-18-2001||11:29 AM||||If you use a DIS coil, you can fire two plugs off of one coil.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FormulaJoe||09-18-2001||04:19 PM||||Why reinvent the wheel?  They have kits to do this, look in the magazines with  older hotrods ('40 and '50's) they have a kit to do it.  There is a guy with an old 50 something Plymouth that shows up regularly at a couple of places I like to cruze.  He puts on a show for everyone, shoots flame several feet out the back of the car.  His finale is a loud bang, sounds like a cannon going off!   I have noticed his pipes protrude several inches past his bumper to spare his chrome and paint.||||reg||6
